{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all","id":1492891,"title":"Do any of you use the Inconnu in your games at all?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-12T09:52:38-07:00","id":1492891,"title":"Do any of you use the Inconnu in your games at all?","content":"Inspired by the True Black Hand Thread earlier. I got to wonder how most of you bother with this group of secretive kindred?<br /> <br /> I pointed out in the previous post that our game that our coterie weren't really sure of there existence and were used as a scapegoat by paraniod elders &amp; ancients when there plans go south because of something they didn't expect.<br /> <br /> So have you ever used them in any fashion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T10:59:21-07:00","id":1492899,"title":"","content":"I like vaguely defined, secretive kindred cults. I mostly run them as guys who wish they ran the Camarilla but can't, but they do influence it. <br /> <br /> But the players are almost always neonates, so they're unfortunately rarely relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T12:08:28-07:00","id":1492908,"title":"","content":"Unlike the TMR, I don't care for the Inconnu at all. I find the Inconnu as unmalleable for story telling and uninteresting for goals. If I was going to remake the Inconnu I think I would make it a 'Right handed path&quot; version of a &quot;Left Handed Path&quot; TMR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12895-mrnatas","name":"MrNatas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12895_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T12:40:46-07:00","id":1492910,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Used them almost in every game I run, but never in the foreground, often through mediators.They are great because even old veterans seldom encounter them and therefore they carry a certain mysticism and their goals can be incredible arcane.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is me, just forgot my PW and changed my email<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25163-crytash2","name":"Crytash2","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25163_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T13:03:37-07:00","id":1492916,"title":"","content":"I include speculation and conspiracy mongering about the Inconnu (as well as other factions) in game by NPCs. But I have never introduced an actual Inconnu NPC meeting the PCs in game. We've not been given sufficient information for them to make them a really interesting faction in my opinion. Someone who &quot;monitors&quot; a city but mostly refrains from any interference doesn't add a lot to a chronicle.<br /> <br /> The &quot;obvious&quot; thing to do with them is make them a potential source about Golconda, but there are other factions out there that can serve the same purpose but be more interesting.<br /> <br /> If I need a mysterious group of elders mucking about, I am more prone to use existing, but seldom used, concepts like the various Gehenna cults mentioned in the Elysium sourcebook, groups like the Children of Osiris, certain coteries/factions name dropped in clanbooks, and the groups I've created myself for my own chronicles.<br /> <br /> If the Inconnu had a more active plan and tactical bent, I'd be willing to use them more. But as written, I'm just not inspired to do anything with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T13:13:43-07:00","id":1492919,"title":"","content":"I have used the Inconnu in a few different ways.<br /> <br /> I had a one off where I ran the factions as political analogs. So the Camarilla &amp; Sabbat were liberal and conservative (reader's choice which was which), the anarchs were millenials and younger generations, while the Inconnu were centrists/independents. For the one off I had condensed things down into an underground city design where it was more political fighting than factions owning cities or territories. The clans were changed to better fit the needs of a vampire city, thus the Nosferatu were a clan of engineers and architects, while the Ventrue were the procurers of unmissed mortals to add to the cities cattle pens, etc. <br /> <br /> I ran a series of games where all vampires were essentially Inconnu. No factions, no Jyhad, just a society of immortals who made their way through unlife as quietly and unnoticed as possible. This was a cross over game so most of the drama came from the other game lines such as Werewolf and Wraith.<br /> <br /> Lastly in the most unmodified version of their use, the Inconnu were used as a goal for the PCs. They wanted to get out of the eternal war and just exist peacefully, thus the mythical Inconnu seemed like a good thing to focus on. The Inconnu is more realistic than say having the entire coterie attain Golconda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-15T21:12:06-07:00","id":1493147,"title":"","content":"I never have, but it may be that I'm just not old school enough. I've always seen them as something created for Chicago By Night, but superseded by cults and sects whose clearer histories, methods, and goals made them more interesting to me by the time I got into the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T00:18:36-07:00","id":1493154,"title":"","content":"If a player doesn't give me a caveat on their 4-5 point mentor I default to inconnu. I had one pretending to be a street preacher looking out for caitiff and thin bloods, he basically acted as a modern ashen priest, no one caught on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T05:27:54-07:00","id":1493159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1493154#post1493154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a player doesn't give me a caveat on their 4-5 point mentor I default to inconnu. I had one pretending to be a street preacher looking out for caitiff and thin bloods, he basically acted as a modern ashen priest, no one caught on.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's wrong with just a really powerful elder/the prince/ the guy who secretly controls the prince/ a group of people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T06:16:03-07:00","id":1493160,"title":"","content":"They aren't in every game I run, but in most of my longer running VtM campaigns, eventually the Inconnu make some sort of appearance. But I also change them up dramatically. Sometimes they're what they are in the books. Sometimes they're actually demon worshippers. Sometimes they're a front for the True Black Hand. Sometimes they're direct agents for an Antediluvian. Sometimes they aren't even vampires (at least not anymore). Basically they're my designated &quot;mystery box&quot; faction in VtM, and I try to change them up and do something different with them to surprise the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T10:25:21-07:00","id":1493169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1493159#post1493159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's wrong with just a really powerful elder/the prince/ the guy who secretly controls the prince/ a group of people?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing but it Tends to be too invested in politics and personal agenda to be worth 5 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T10:33:02-07:00","id":1493172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1493169#post1493169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing but it Tends to be too invested in politics and personal agenda to be worth 5 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not to mention it overly complicates the ongoing plot and there is something good about keeping things simple when it comes to storytelling and you might not have the skill to pull it off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T23:48:49-07:00","id":1493202,"title":"","content":"I use them with some frequency.<br /> <br /> What the Inconnu offers over any other group is that their core is very, very simple. And importantly, it isn't just vague, but really simple. It can be a lot of things, but it only <i>need</i> to be a bunch of drop-outs from the Jyhad. You can make them into whatever you want, or just take at face value and you're ready to go.<br /> <br /> This simplicity means you can have almost any concept in the form of an Inconnu without breaking anything nor having to delve into more complex explanations than you're going to actually use. A mastermind that works outside the sects, a dupe used by them, any age, clan, Generation or political view, any level of any Path, with whatever connections you want with other characters in the game. It is extremely versatile and without unneeded baggage for the ST to deal with.<br /> <br /> Such versatility is really good to default a character you don't want to be directly involved with the main political conflicts of your game. Be it a mentor that can offer insight to the PCs, someone you like to have mostly as background, a villain to be faced at some point or an ally the characters must struggle to win over. It may be a &quot;placeholder&quot; for a new concept you have for the group or just an option to place and name a truly independent (on the surface) character. You may even have it undefined until later if that fits your needs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-01T13:08:32-07:00","id":1521831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1492916#post1492916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've not been given sufficient information for them to make them a really interesting faction in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I was rereading some sections of Children of the Inquisition for the other thread on Dracula's diablerie of Tabak, I noticed something that I thought was quite relevant to this thread which I remembered.<br /> <br /> In chapter on Dracula (page 18), it provides this bit of information concerning the Inconnu that I cannot recall being mentioned anywhere else:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Children of the Inquisition</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eventually Dracula joined the independent sect of respected vampire elders called the Inconnu, who worked ceaselessly to cure vampires of their need for blood. In their quest for greater knowledge, these vampires allied themselves with demons. But then, Dracula always did make a career out of trading one evil for another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does anybody recall similar language elsewhere? Reading it, it changes how I think about the Inconnu.<br /> <br /> Working to cure vampires of their need to blood doesn't exactly sound like Golconda. Although achieving Golconda can be one aspect of that search, it is definitely not the same thing as vampire never needing blood again. So that would greatly expand the Inconnu from a group of elders searching for the secrets of Golconda (which I and I think many other players merely see them as doing), and into a society of elders wanting to exploring the general nature of the Kindred existence and seeking to eliminate negative aspects of their curse. That includes reducing or eliminating their need to drink blood, but also maybe eliminating the danger from sunlight, preventing themselves falling into torpor, removing the need to drink vampire vitae later on as they age, and lots of other things as well. It could also mean information that allows them to return to being a mortal. <br /> <br /> It doesn't mean all Inconnu members want them exact same thing, but it does mean all of them want to better understand their vampiric condition and looking at a way to improve it.<br /> <br /> That transforms the sect from being mostly passive, into a more active one investigating a lot of mysteries, experimenting, contacting dangerous spirits in the search for answers, etc. That might also mean active investigation into the whereabouts of Caine and the Antedeluvians, who could know a lot more about the nature of vampirism, not to destroy them, but to learn from them. So they are doing lots of things as well. That could explain why they have Monitors in cities. Not only does that allow them to observe potential recruits, it is not a passive monitoring. They are looking for clues that could help them and their sect for the specific knowledge that helps them. And lots of things might potentially be interesting to them - Tremere experiments with blood, the activities of the Salubri, Noddist scholars uncovering new information, and lots more.<br /> <br /> I think I will be revising my understanding of the Inconnu for my chronicles based on this. I might even begin including them in my chronicles in some capacity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-03T12:33:33-07:00","id":1521997,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s something we should consider in our game Blackfox if and when we will include agents of the Inconnu and it will the founder of one of character line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T21:53:14-07:00","id":1522137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1521831#post1521831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I was rereading some sections of Children of the Inquisition for the other thread on Dracula's diablerie of Tabak, I noticed something that I thought was quite relevant to this thread which I remembered.<br /> <br /> In chapter on Dracula (page 18), it provides this bit of information concerning the Inconnu that I cannot recall being mentioned anywhere else:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Does anybody recall similar language elsewhere? Reading it, it changes how I think about the Inconnu.<br /> <br /> Working to cure vampires of their need to blood doesn't exactly sound like Golconda. Although achieving Golconda can be one aspect of that search, it is definitely not the same thing as vampire never needing blood again. So that would greatly expand the Inconnu from a group of elders searching for the secrets of Golconda (which I and I think many other players merely see them as doing), and into a society of elders wanting to exploring the general nature of the Kindred existence and seeking to eliminate negative aspects of their curse. That includes reducing or eliminating their need to drink blood, but also maybe eliminating the danger from sunlight, preventing themselves falling into torpor, removing the need to drink vampire vitae later on as they age, and lots of other things as well. It could also mean information that allows them to return to being a mortal.<br /> <br /> It doesn't mean all Inconnu members want them exact same thing, but it does mean all of them want to better understand their vampiric condition and looking at a way to improve it.<br /> <br /> That transforms the sect from being mostly passive, into a more active one investigating a lot of mysteries, experimenting, contacting dangerous spirits in the search for answers, etc. That might also mean active investigation into the whereabouts of Caine and the Antedeluvians, who could know a lot more about the nature of vampirism, not to destroy them, but to learn from them. So they are doing lots of things as well. That could explain why they have Monitors in cities. Not only does that allow them to observe potential recruits, it is not a passive monitoring. They are looking for clues that could help them and their sect for the specific knowledge that helps them. And lots of things might potentially be interesting to them - Tremere experiments with blood, the activities of the Salubri, Noddist scholars uncovering new information, and lots more.<br /> <br /> I think I will be revising my understanding of the Inconnu for my chronicles based on this. I might even begin including them in my chronicles in some capacity.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very interesting way to look at the Inconnu. Their preoccupations can be myriad and idiosyncratic, but they are united by their desire to &quot;solve&quot; vampirism, as a general goal. What &quot;solving vampirism&quot; means depends on the Inconnu member, which lends them to a number of different character and narrative dynamics, and many plot hooks.<br /> <br /> It feeds in my conception of the sect as being of vampires who seek, above all, an &quot;Alternate Win Condition&quot; for the Jyhad, to use a term from games like Magic: The Gathering. Trying to struggle with other vampires for power, influence, and pride is a sucker's game. In trying to dominate your fellow lick, you get dominated (or Dominated) in turn, usually by older, more powerful Kindred. The need to secure blood, evade vampiric banes, and maintain a base of power and safety all make a Kindred vulnerable. Trying to &quot;win&quot; the Jyhad through accumulating power, and eliminating or subborning all rivals, is impossible for all but the Antedeluvians (if even they can &quot;win&quot;).<br /> <br /> Finding ways to circumvent or transcend the vampiric condition - to push beyond the boundaries of one's nature - is itself a means of circumventing or transcending the Jyhad. You need never struggle with your peers for feeding rights, if you no longer require blood. Etc, etc. Whether this is through Golconda - whatever that is - or through some more esoteric function.<br /> <br /> It's also for this reason why, though their goals may differ, the Inconnu generally don't war against each other. Getting into slap-fights with other Kindred is, to the Inconnu, a waste of time and effort. It's why the excused themselves from the Jyhad at large. Conflicts may still break out, but it's the exception rather than the norm. The result of Inconnu members judging the means or ends of another to be so unacceptable that intercession, or even violence, is necessary.<br /> <br /> The Inconnu gather lore and keep it secret for twin reasons. First because any scrap of data could be calamitous (or at least inconvenient) if it falls into the wrong hands. Whether it's those outside the Inconnu, or rival factions within it. Second, that same scrap of data could be the key to unraveling the mysteries of vampirism. The lynchpin of some Inconnu member's chosen &quot;win con&quot;. And so hoarding information and keeping it dispersed is an important function of the sect, as is gathering more of it. But Inconnu must also pool information at times, as they pool resources, to further their ends.<br /> <br /> So the Inconnu, in practice, is a mix of hierarchical and cellular. Members using agents to monitor the Jyhad for answers and as go-betweens with other Inconnu. They don't get involved in wars where they can help it, because they seek &quot;victory&quot; through end-running vampirism itself. But any given Inconnu is not necessarily &quot;good&quot; in the traditional sense, just because they mind their own business as a general rule. The form of transcendence they seek may not be pleasant, and the means to get there may be even less so. So they can easily be slotted into an antagonist role, albeit one the Coterie is unlikely to encounter until well into the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-05T23:08:06-07:00","id":1522139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1522137#post1522137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very interesting way to look at the Inconnu. Their preoccupations can be myriad and idiosyncratic, but they are united by their desire to &quot;solve&quot; vampirism, as a general goal. What &quot;solving vampirism&quot; means depends on the Inconnu member, which lends them to a number of different character and narrative dynamics, and many plot hooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I thought too. It's amazing how one little sentence can transform the way one can look upon the sect. I'm pleasantly surprised that the post already has lots of Likes. So I think it's inspiring other people too. I have no idea if this was the secret intention of Greenberg and the other original writers of VtM, but it makes sense to me and is definitely something I can use in my games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1522137#post1522137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finding ways to circumvent or transcend the vampiric condition - to push beyond the boundaries of one's nature - is itself a means of circumventing or transcending the Jyhad. You need never struggle with your peers for feeding rights, if you no longer require blood. Etc, etc. Whether this is through Golconda - whatever that is - or through some more esoteric function.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this because not only does it reflect upon other knowledge we know about the Inconnu (namely their interest in Golconda and the screwed up situation in Hunedoara Castle), but it also meshes with other ideas already existing in the VtM setting. The idea of metamorphosis and transcendence is documented in lots of other places in VtM lore. It's not coming out of nowhere. This is the kind of long term, even metaphysical thinking, we see in a lot of ancient vampires and certain Gehenna cults.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1522137#post1522137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Inconnu, in practice, is a mix of hierarchical and cellular. Members using agents to monitor the Jyhad for answers and as go-betweens with other Inconnu. They don't get involved in wars where they can help it, because they seek &quot;victory&quot; through end-running vampirism itself. But any given Inconnu is not necessarily &quot;good&quot; in the traditional sense, just because they mind their own business as a general rule. The form of transcendence they seek may not be pleasant, and the means to get there may be even less so. So they can easily be slotted into an antagonist role, albeit one the Coterie is unlikely to encounter until well into the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main advantage to me is that it now makes the Inconnu a group that is actively doing something for an understandable reason. They are not passive. And their goals are not unknowable. That helps me tremendously as an ST. But this is something an ST can easily keep under their belt, informing how they run the sect in the game, but still have it be unknown to the PCs. It keeps the traditional information known about the sect as is, but allows an ST to do other things with individual members if they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T01:19:17-07:00","id":1522142,"title":"","content":"Personally the Inconnu don't make anything for me and I actually don't seem any use of them that wouldn't just make things more convuluted to keep track of and engage with plots within plots and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T10:45:48-07:00","id":1522163,"title":"","content":"I have to admit that your little post on how you view the Inconnu Black Fox certainly sparked some interest and my Golden State Warriors hat is off to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T11:29:30-07:00","id":1522171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1522163#post1522163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to admit that your little post on how you view the Inconnu Black Fox certainly sparked some interest and my Golden State Warriors hat is off to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. I am considering introducing the Inconnu in my current game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T14:41:40-07:00","id":1522183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1521831#post1521831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Working to cure vampires of their need to blood doesn't exactly sound like Golconda. Although achieving Golconda can be one aspect of that search, it is definitely not the same thing as vampire never needing blood again. So that would greatly expand the Inconnu from a group of elders searching for the secrets of Golconda (which I and I think many other players merely see them as doing), and into a society of elders wanting to exploring the general nature of the Kindred existence and seeking to eliminate negative aspects of their curse. That includes reducing or eliminating their need to drink blood, but also maybe eliminating the danger from sunlight, preventing themselves falling into torpor, removing the need to drink vampire vitae later on as they age, and lots of other things as well. It could also mean information that allows them to return to being a mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That should make them <i>very </i>invested in the Children of Osiris, Bardo seems like a tailor-made Discipline for them. <i>Children of the Inquisition</i> is also 1e era, right? I don't remember if <i>Hunters Hunted</i> came before or after, but I wonder if the two are related in some way.<br /> At the very least, it could provide some alternative explanations for the disappearance of the bloodline.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T19:29:30-07:00","id":1522198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1522183#post1522183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That should make them <i>very </i>invested in the Children of Osiris, Bardo seems like a tailor-made Discipline for them. <i>Children of the Inquisition</i> is also 1e era, right? I don't remember if <i>Hunters Hunted</i> came before or after, but I wonder if the two are related in some way.<br /> At the very least, it could provide some alternative explanations for the disappearance of the bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the main sticking point for Golconda seekers, vis a vis Bardo, is that it's not really a &quot;win condition&quot; to use my earlier terminology. Bardo allows you to curb the worst aspects of the vampiric condition, but only through great personal effort and restraint, and a complete dedication to a certain unlifestyle. If you follow the path laid by the Children of Osiris, you're signing up for an eternity of aestheticism. All with the knowledge that you're only managing the curse, not overcoming it.<br /> <br /> It's not a bad gig, if you can get it. There are worse ways to spend eternity, and ones far less moral. But not to the taste of someone who wants to exit the vampirism game entirely (while still sticking around in the world, of course; catching a sunrise is always an option if you're REALLY sick of being a vampire).<br /> <br /> To someone of the Inconnu, Bardo can be a useful tool to pursue, but it's ultimately a stopgap. Maintaining high Humanity has its benefits and lets you sleep more easily at day, but you're not &quot;winning&quot; the Jyhad or escaping the curse. Golconda promises true release, though what that means is vague and poorly understood.<br /> <br /> The difference between Bardo and Golconda is like the difference between living an aesthetic lifestyle to limit the bad karma you do, and achieving Enlightenment and escaping Samsara. While the former is admirable, from a Buddhist standpoint, you're really aiming for the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-06T23:32:14-07:00","id":1522202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1522198#post1522198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main sticking point for Golconda seekers, vis a vis Bardo, is that it's not really a &quot;win condition&quot; to use my earlier terminology. Bardo allows you to curb the worst aspects of the vampiric condition, but only through great personal effort and restraint, and a complete dedication to a certain unlifestyle. If you follow the path laid by the Children of Osiris, you're signing up for an eternity of aestheticism. All with the knowledge that you're only managing the curse, not overcoming it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think the Inconnus would be interested in monitoring the Children of Osiris, but reach the same conclusion about Bardo as you laid out. Bardo can be useful, but ultimately does not lead to the overcoming of vampiric limitations. Some members of the Inconnu might be attracted to it, but the sect as a whole would not.<br /> <br /> At the same time, there could be a sense if that the Children of Osiris achieved this result, then maybe they might achieve some future result that is more compelling to the Inconnu.<br /> <br /> So in the meantime, treat them like they do others - do not interfere, monitor, and report anything useful.<br /> <br /> The hard part, of course, is that Children of Osiris would not want to be monitored anymore by the Inconnu than by any other vampiric group.<br /> <br /> I consider groups like the Inconnu and Children of Osiris to be operating at the same level of &quot;high Jyhad&quot;. They are peers even if the Inconnu is larger, more powerful, and better known. These groups don't manipulate each other. They manipulate groups/sects that operate at a lower level of the Jyhad then them. The Children of Osiris should be cognizant enough to keep most of their activities secret even by a sect like the Inconnu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T03:46:04-07:00","id":1522209,"title":"","content":"I agree that Bardo (and the Children of Osirises paradigm as ascetics) would not be seen as a ultimate goal, but rather a possible venue. Which is an interesting point, because individual members of the Inconnu then could have vastly different opinions while sharing the same goal. For example, a Tzimisce Metamorphist could go the complete opposite direction and lean into the vampiric condition, with transcendence of the vampiric negatives as an endpoint in mastery of the state. A blood sorcerer could go at it from an angle that is completely divorced from 'unlivestyle' and simply a question of arcane mastery.<br /> <br /> The effect of this is that the sect as a whole would be devoid of a moral baseline - pursuing their goals as saints, monsters, or neither doesn't matter. I like that thought because it explains why the sect acts like it does, focusing on observation rather than action. At the same time, it would imply that they would have difficulty to make consensual moves as an organization when necessary. I have to re-read the chapter in Beckett's Jyhad Diary with the ex-Inconnu, IIRC it has some description of the internal organization and stuff like consensus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T14:10:38-07:00","id":1522233,"title":"","content":"Quick question. Was this Children of Osirsis bloodline ever a major faction in the older settings of Vampire The Masquerade or a poorly defined idea that never got fleshed out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-07T14:57:28-07:00","id":1522238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1522233#post1522233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question. Was this Children of Osirsis bloodline ever a major faction in the older settings of Vampire The Masquerade or a poorly defined idea that never got fleshed out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Somewhere in between, to be honest. The bloodline itself was set up to be a major antagonist to the Setites which aside from supplements that directly deal with them or the area got little attention, but the organization as a whole gained more prominence in other splats when it was paired with the Cult of Isis. Most of the meat for it actually comes from (early) Mummy and Mage, and the former gradually moved away from them as a vampire organization while the latter (together with Werewolf) focused more on the Cult of Isis.<br /> So, lore-wise they were actually a pretty important faction until they got removed from the setting, even if they didn't receive much material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T10:52:16-07:00","id":1522273,"title":"","content":"Thank you Voidshaper.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-08T16:53:45-07:00","id":1522285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1492891-do-any-of-you-use-the-inconnu-in-your-games-at-all?p=1522233#post1522233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question. Was this Children of Osirsis bloodline ever a major faction in the older settings of Vampire The Masquerade or a poorly defined idea that never got fleshed out?</div> </div> </div> </div>There were very few mentions of the Children of Osiris in the sourcebooks. They were mentioned early in the original Hunters Hunted. They were actually never referred to as a bloodline (and their members in fact, do not embrace new childer), but because they were given a unique Discipline, Bardo, people began referring to them as a Bloodline, and that was soon how they were mentioned in subsequent sourcebooks. But they are more like a (monastic) sect.<br /> <br /> Since they were mentioned as one of the Hunter groups, it seems to me they were meant to be antagonists in the setting. Unlike even the Salubri, mentioned in the Players Guide, they weren't meant as a PC option, but a tool for the ST.<br /> <br /> The Children of Osiris would continue to be mentioned in a few subsequent sourcebooks, but not too much. I think outside of Hunters Hunted they got the most mentioned in the Kemintiri chapter of Kindred Most Wanted for 1e/2e. So except for those people who managed to buy the original Hunters Hunted, I think most VtM players only heard about them from third parties. Hunters Hunted was an early sourcebook, and I don't remember new copies arriving in game stores after the run sold out. It was a very early product and didn't look as professional as the 2e products. This was pre-PDF days, pre-Internet stores, so unless you picked up a used copy at some used book store or game store, you had very little information on them to go by.<br /> <br /> Because they were seen as &quot;good guys&quot; vampires, they got purged out of existence in the Revised era (along with a lot of other things).<br /> <br /> If you want a rundown on the Children of Osiris, they were discussed on a thread, often comparing them to the Salubri, some years ago. The thread ended up being very useful to me, so I'll share it <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1450257-children-of-osiris\">here</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T10:37:45-07:00","id":1522305,"title":"","content":"Good guy vampires is a contadiction in this setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T14:43:20-07:00","id":1522311,"title":"","content":"While I firmly believe that vampires are monsters and should all be destroyed, there are many examples in the genre of reluctant vampires who try to hold onto their humanity and avoid evil acts. Barnabas Collins from Dark Shadows TV show, Hannibal King in Marvel's Tomb of Dracula comic book, Louis from Anne Rice's novels, Nick Knight from Forever Knight. I think even Marie from Innocent Blood and Caleb &amp; Mae from Near Dark qualify. So I think it's OK to have them in the setting. Just make it clear these are very rare exceptions, and over time their numbers dwindle.<br /> <br /> So I don't even mind if there are maybe two or three dozen or so vampires who exist in some kind of monastic order trying to limit the harm they do. The Children of Osiris are probably not a setting element that should appear in every chronicle or without reason. But it can make sense for them to make an actual presence in certain chronicles if done correctly. <br /> <br /> But the Revised era was less about providing tools for individual STs to use in their own chronicles, and more about trying to force everyone to play in a specific chronicle designed by one person (or a small group of people working together). No matter how much fun some people might think that one chronicle was, it was a mutilating limitation to the game. If players didn't want the Children of Osiris, or the Tal'Mahe'Ra or any other element in the setting, they already had the power to simply not mention them or even erase them in their own chronicles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-09T21:56:44-07:00","id":1522327,"title":"","content":"Nope; never used them once. But most of my Vamp-games were focused on the essence of being a vampire, the Beast and being supernatural, and not revolving around politics too much. I never liked the mega-plots; I'm not one for mega-plots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T04:39:52-07:00","id":1522339,"title":"","content":"I use the Ordo Dracul instead","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-10T12:47:46-07:00","id":1522353,"title":"","content":"I could never get into Ordo Dracul in the other setting, I was more Invictus, Circle Of The Crone and Carthians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}